      "type": "action",
      "img": "icons/magic/light/beam-impact-deflect-teal.webp",
      "system": {
        "active": true,
        "description": "<p class=\"feature\"><em>Trigger:</em> The stone giant is hit by a ranged attack roll and takes Bludgeoning, Piercing, or Slashing damage from it.</p><p class=\"feature\"><em>Response:</em> The stone giant reduces the damage it takes from the attack by 5 (1d10) Healing, and if that damage is reduced to 0, the stone giant can redirect some of the attack's force.</p><p class=\"feature\"><em>Dexterity Saving Throw:</em> DC 17, one creature the stone giant can see within 60 feet. </p><p class=\"feature\"><em>Failure:</em> 11 (1d10 + 6) Force damage.</p>",
